{"content":[{"c":["SHELAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Arphaxad’s son and the father of Eber (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.24","r":"Gen.10.24","rawR":"Gen.10.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.24","value":"Gen.10.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.12-15","r":"Gen.11.12-15","rawR":"Gen.11.12-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.12-15","value":"Gen.11.12-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:12-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.18","r":"1Chr.1.18","rawR":"1Chr.1.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.18","value":"1Chr.1.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:18"},"). Shelah is listed in Luke’s genealogy of Christ as the son of Cainan the son of Arphaxad (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.35","r":"Luke.3.35","rawR":"Luke.3.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.35","value":"Luke.3.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:35"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Judah’s third son by Bathshua the Canaanitess. He was born at Kezib, a small town in Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.5","r":"Gen.38.5","rawR":"Gen.38.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.5","value":"Gen.38.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.3","r":"1Chr.2.3","rawR":"1Chr.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.3","value":"1Chr.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:3"},"). Shelah founded the Shelanite family (",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.20","r":"Num.26.20","rawR":"Num.26.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.20","value":"Num.26.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:20"},"), which should possibly be read instead of “Shilonite” in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.5","r":"Neh.11.5","rawR":"Neh.11.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.5","value":"Neh.11.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 11:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.5","r":"1Chr.9.5","rawR":"1Chr.9.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.5","value":"1Chr.9.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 9:5"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shelah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.24"},{"anchorText":"11:12-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.12-15","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.12-15","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.12-15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.18","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.18","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.18"},{"anchorText":"Lk 3:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.35","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.35","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.35"},{"anchorText":"Gn 38:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.3","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.3","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.3"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.20","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.20","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.20"},{"anchorText":"Nehemiah 11:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.5","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.5","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 9:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"28060186e6d25c2592d7d0f0bda71f6f0761c2c13727214758a5888256f9837c","sourceItemName":"Shelah